WEBVTT

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:03.810
What? They won't be able to escape the pack?

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:07.610
Yeah, even if they do make it to the pack.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.490
Leaving the pack is fairly difficult.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:14.820
Is it really impossible?

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:19.330
It's a different story if he's 
made special preparations.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:22.550
Special preparations?

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:27.690
Kaburagi, do you want to leave 
the pack, no matter what?

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:30.430
Of course, damn it.

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:33.000
What if there was a way?

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:33.590
Huh?

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:36.530
Do you have something?

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.120
I wasn't expecting to use this here.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.240
I'll do anything.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:43.230
Tell me!

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:48.750
It's this.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:52.190
G-God's stationery?

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:54.130
I knew God would come through.

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:56.230
He's written a hint on it.

00:00:56.230 --> 00:01:00.360
The princess...?

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.580
Those are the lyrics to a certain song.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.140
"You are the princess"?

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.630
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:16.720
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:39.180
Lyrics?

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:43.600
Does that mean there's a hint hidden in them?

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:44.700
<i>LINE.10  #16, Shinkai Yuto</i>

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.500
"White?"

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:46.830
"Tee hee hee?"

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:50.470
"Even with a spell to make you bigger?"

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:51.790
A spell?

00:02:51.790 --> 00:02:53.220
"Princess, Princess"?

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:54.110
Princess?!

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:56.320
What the hell does "Princess" mean?

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:59.570
Wait, there's no point in asking Aoyagi.

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:04.050
Princess... Pony... Hooves?

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.430
Run like a horse?

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.330
No, no, no...

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:08.580
Hill climb?

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:12.190
This command from God is 
too difficult to understand!

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:13.380
I don't get it!

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.940
Will this really help us get out of the pack?

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:20.220
Kaburagi, those are song lyrics.

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:22.920
I know that. You just said—

00:03:22.920 --> 00:03:24.700
You don't read lyrics.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:25.850
You sing them.

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:28.050
Sing?

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:31.410
You want me to sing?

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:32.980
These frou-frou lyrics?

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:36.550
And the way these sentences are written...

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:38.020
This is definitely a girl's song.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:39.650
And you want me to sing it?

00:03:40.430 --> 00:03:41.370
That's right.

00:03:42.010 --> 00:03:43.070
And that's...

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:48.950
The opening theme of last year's
super-popular bishoujo anime, <i>Love Hime</i>!

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:51.250
What are you talking about, Aoyagi-san?!

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:55.040
There's a star between <i>Love</i> and <i>Hime</i>.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:58.140
Is that important? Is that really important?!

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.290
What's wrong, Aoyagi? Are you okay?

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:02.060
Has the heat gotten to you?

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:03.570
Poor Aoyagi...

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:06.050
Wait, did you watch that anime?

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:09.330
I've never seen it, but I've sung the song.

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:13.770
Over and over again.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:17.270
<b>Sohoku
High
School
Bicycle
Club</b>

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:17.270
What did you want to discuss?

00:04:17.270 --> 00:04:20.290
My last race as a third-year is over,

00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:23.200
and I've come to a good stopping 
point in studying for my exams.

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:29.740
There's something I forgot to tell you guys.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:34.030
Is it important?

00:04:34.030 --> 00:04:36.680
It is. Listen closely.

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:37.370
Yes, sir.

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:42.420
<i>A message from Tadokoro-san, an
 established sprinter, to me, an aspiring one.</i>

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:51.820
Learn this anime song.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:52.990
Huh? What?

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:54.060
What? What?!

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:56.560
Learn this anime song!

00:04:58.270 --> 00:04:59.020
What?

00:04:59.290 --> 00:05:03.530
<b>Love Hime</b>

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:01.340
It's an anime called <i>Love Hime</i>.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:02.780
I have the CD.

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:06.280
There's a star between <i>Love</i> and <i>Hime</i>.

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:08.590
Apparently, that's important.

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:11.540
The star spins during the opening song.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:14.830
Apparently, it grows larger and shrinks, too.

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:18.420
Onoda taught me this song.

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:24.420
During the second stage of the Inter-High!

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:32.970
Thanks to this song, we were able to 
catch up to Kinjou and the team last year.

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:36.490
Road races are long,
 both in distance and duration.

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:39.230
Unexpected events occur one after another.

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:43.260
There's no way to prepare for everything.

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:46.650
But you do what you can.

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:52.370
If it increases your chances of 
winning by even 1%, you can't compromise.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:54.200
You have to do it.

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:58.790
Even if at first glance it seems meaningless.

00:05:59.390 --> 00:06:03.670
Honestly, I doubt this song will 
be sung at the Inter-High again.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:20.560
<b>Love Hime</b>

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:10.410
You can ask me what it's good for,
 but I can only tell you that I don't know.

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:17.410
But this anime song I'd never heard 
before lead Sohoku to victory.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:20.560
It made us come together as one.

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:24.310
<i>Tadokoro-san...</i>

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:27.780
<i>He's serious.</i>

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:37.080
It might be a common occurrence, 
but it's important to girls!

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:33.940
He suddenly started singing!

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:41.210
Are my feelings reaching you?

00:06:37.950 --> 00:06:39.890
A-Aoyagi-san!

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:45.490
Are they not?

00:06:45.490 --> 00:06:49.220
<i>Tadokoro-san used this song 
to return to the team!</i>

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:51.130
One of them started singing.

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:52.640
What is that?

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.750
This is embarrassing, Aoyagi-san!

00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:56.260
Everyone's looking at us!

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:58.810
I can't believe you're singing so loudly!

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:01.020
Princess, Princess! Princess!

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:03.040
I love, love, love you!

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:04.520
Princess! Princess!

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.060
Twinkle, twinkle!

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:07.020
Stop, Aoyagi!

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:09.530
Even with a spell to make you bigger!

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:11.030
Seriously, give me a break!

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:14.780
You're still my princess, 
you are who you are!

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:14.780
Princesses and magic are so lame!

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:18.080
That's the most important part.

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:20.410
Did you get all that?

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:26.810
<i>He's serious...</i>

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:33.010
Were you lying when you said you'd 
do anything to escape the pack?

00:07:34.110 --> 00:07:38.390
Would you refuse to sing this song, 
even if it increased your chance by 1%?

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:41.380
No way! It can't do that!

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:42.850
Calm down!

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:44.900
It's a song! An anime song, no less!

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:45.940
There's no way it'll help!

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:49.090
I don't know if it will or won't.

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:53.370
But you can't know for 
certain until you try it!

00:07:54.230 --> 00:07:56.870
<i>Sing loudly in the middle of the pack?</i>

00:07:57.730 --> 00:07:59.750
<i>He's out of his mind!</i>

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:03.170
<i>But Aoyagi is serious.</i>

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.380
<i>How can I know when I haven't tried it?</i>

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:07.960
<i>He's right.</i>

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:10.160
<i>Damn it! I don't believe this!</i>

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:11.380
<i>I don't get it!</i>

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:16.180
<i>But remember, this is a note from God.</i>

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:20.510
<i>If this will help me move forward...</i>

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:24.630
Okay!

00:08:24.630 --> 00:08:26.060
I'm a man!

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:29.190
I'll sing the anime song!

00:08:29.190 --> 00:08:31.470
As loud as I can!

00:08:31.470 --> 00:08:33.400
Keep singing!

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:35.200
We'll escape the pack!

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:38.780
Match your gears and cadence 
to the song's rhythm and mine!

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:39.690
Yes, sir!

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:41.070
"Princess, Princess!"

00:08:41.070 --> 00:08:42.180
Go!

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:43.750
Princess, Princess!

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:46.180
Now they're singing together.

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:47.740
We're in the middle of a race.

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:52.800
<i>Seriously? This is really embarrassing 
when you sing it out loud!</i>

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:55.890
"Lovely chance pancake girl!"

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:56.500
Go!

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:59.910
L-Lovely chance pancake girl...

00:08:59.910 --> 00:09:01.140
Seriously?

00:09:02.010 --> 00:09:05.140
Okay, one more time from the top!

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:07.030
Huh? Uh, yes, sir!

00:09:07.030 --> 00:09:10.020
<i>We're singing this song more than once?</i>

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:11.860
"Princess, Princess!"

00:09:11.860 --> 00:09:12.560
Go!

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:14.370
Princess, Princess!

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:16.560
Stop, Sohoku.

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:17.610
My stomach hurts.

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:20.140
I love, love, love you!

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:21.630
Princess! Princess!

00:09:21.630 --> 00:09:24.220
I-I love, love, love you!

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:26.290
Princess! Princess!

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:27.950
<i>Damn. Damn!</i>

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:29.590
<i>This is so lame!</i>

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:31.820
<i>Singing out loud...</i>

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:34.210
<i>This is so embarrassing!</i>

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:38.220
"Even with a spell to make you bigger!"

00:09:39.070 --> 00:09:42.850
<i>But I'm racing right now.</i>

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:45.670
"You're still my princess!"

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:46.140
Go!

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:51.690
<i>Not fighting during a race 
would be even lamer!</i>

00:09:52.250 --> 00:09:55.710
You're still my princess!

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:55.710
I can't hear you!

00:09:55.710 --> 00:09:58.000
You are who you are!

00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:58.660
Yes, sir!

00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:01.920
You are who you are!

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:02.880
Sohoku's pulling ahead!

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:03.660
They're trying to leave?

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:05.020
There's no way!

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:06.710
They'll fall back again!

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:10.250
Lovely chance pancake girl!

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:13.580
Lovely chance pancake...

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:15.270
Keep at it, Kaburagi!

00:10:15.270 --> 00:10:18.590
If you stop pedaling now,
 you'll fall back into the pack!

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:25.430
The important thing about using
 it is to sing the whole thing

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:31.750
I don't know why, but you'll 
move farther that way.

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:34.480
Kaburagi, focus!

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:36.230
Forget what's behind you!

00:10:36.230 --> 00:10:38.110
Focus on the song!

00:10:39.220 --> 00:10:40.390
<i>On the song?</i>

00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:43.310
<i>Your instructions are insane, Aoyagi.</i>

00:10:43.310 --> 00:10:47.390
<i>But I'll do it if it'll make me move forward!</i>

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:50.370
Got it!

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:54.050
"Even with a spell to make you bigger!"

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:54.670
Go!

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:59.150
Even with a spell to make you bigger!

00:10:59.150 --> 00:11:01.380
"You're still my princess!"

00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:02.260
Go!

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:05.050
You're still my princess!

00:11:05.050 --> 00:11:07.140
Sing from your stomach!

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:08.640
Yes, sir!

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:10.700
We're breaking through!

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:12.060
Yes, sir!

00:11:12.370 --> 00:11:16.980
You are who you are!

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:22.240
Princess!

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:24.090
They escaped!

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:26.410
What was that weird song?

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:31.050
<i>Tadokoro-san, the song helped!</i>

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:33.580
<i>Just you wait, Junta.</i>

00:11:34.070 --> 00:11:36.420
<i>I promise I'll bring him back to the team!</i>

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:41.470
Love Hime, fight!

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:47.720
I see Sohoku in front of us.

00:11:51.300 --> 00:11:53.850
Can I go after them?

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:57.030
Yeah. Take them out.

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:05.370
Teshima-san, they're coming!

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:08.030
Hakone Academy is closing in on us!

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:11.910
Yeah, but Imaizumi and Naruko are close.

00:12:12.280 --> 00:12:15.560
If we keep going, we should reach them first!

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:16.170
Yes, sir!

00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:20.270
<i>We'll meet up with them as 
long as nothing happens.</i>

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:26.410
In that case, I'm off, Izumida-san!

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:30.870
Yeah. They're trying to 
reach the front before us.

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:33.690
Go shatter their spirits...

00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:35.560
Shinkai Yuto!

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:41.360
I'm finally coming, Mountain King.

00:12:47.390 --> 00:12:50.660
<i>To my race against you!</i>

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:55.010
How can he climb so fast?

00:12:55.010 --> 00:12:57.670
He got 200 meters ahead 
in the blink of an eye.

00:12:58.070 --> 00:13:02.510
Does that idiot always climb 
so fast when he's alone?

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:06.670
Climbers creep me out.

00:13:08.460 --> 00:13:10.180
<i>I'll catch up to you.</i>

00:13:10.770 --> 00:13:12.100
<i>Soon!</i>

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:14.980
One Hakone Academy rider is coming!

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:19.990
<i>What is this? His pressure is incredible...</i>

00:13:19.990 --> 00:13:21.070
<i>Who is it?</i>

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:23.060
<i>That's...</i>

00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:27.570
#16! It's Shinkai-kun!

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:30.200
Gotcha!

00:13:31.590 --> 00:13:32.700
He's fast!

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:35.030
<i>Is he's trying to catch up 
to the front by himself?</i>

00:13:35.780 --> 00:13:37.620
<i>No, those eyes...</i>

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:38.990
Yeah!

00:13:38.990 --> 00:13:40.750
<i>He's trying to take us out!</i>

00:13:42.490 --> 00:13:43.460
We don't have a choice.

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:46.260
Go, Onoda! Alone!

00:13:46.730 --> 00:13:47.590
What?

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:53.220
They're trying to use #16 to 
stop us and reach the front first!

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:55.650
You have to go on alone!

00:13:55.650 --> 00:13:57.310
What about you?

00:13:58.950 --> 00:14:01.690
I'll stop him! I'll form a wall!

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:08.150
Ride as hard as you can to 
reach Imaizumi and Naruko!

00:14:10.110 --> 00:14:10.910
Yes, sir!

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:13.580
Go, Onoda!

00:14:14.630 --> 00:14:15.820
Yes, sir!

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:20.590
<i>#16 is coming.</i>

00:14:20.590 --> 00:14:22.850
<i>He didn't do much yesterday.</i>

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:25.750
<i>His strength is unknown.</i>

00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:29.130
<i>But he's a regular on Hakone 
Academy's team as a first-year.</i>

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:33.220
<i>That alone tells me he's unbelievably strong.</i>

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:37.470
<i>And he's the younger 
brother of Shinkai Hayato,</i>

00:14:37.470 --> 00:14:40.060
<i>Hakone Academy's ace sprinter last year.</i>

00:14:40.890 --> 00:14:44.550
<i>The data we have on him is 
so good it makes me sick.</i>

00:14:45.340 --> 00:14:46.150
<i>But...</i>

00:14:47.510 --> 00:14:48.960
<i>I'll stop him!</i>

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:52.910
<i>I've teamed up with Aoyagi countless 
times to claim the winner's podium!</i>

00:14:53.590 --> 00:14:55.740
Run, Onoda!

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:59.660
I'll form a wall and stop him!

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:04.520
<i>What happened?</i>

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:06.340
<i>He was heading straight forward.</i>

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:10.440
<i>But he changed his course at 
the last second to pass me.</i>

00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:16.150
<i>On top of that, he drove his wheel towards 
the right and faked a pass on my right side.</i>

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:23.480
<i>His bike control is unbelievably fast!</i>

00:15:23.870 --> 00:15:27.440
But we have our own plans!

00:15:28.230 --> 00:15:31.570
<i>I've heard about him at races 
from other guys from Kanagawa.</i>

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:38.540
<i>They call Shinkai Hayato's brother the 
Peak Hornet, the hornet of the summit.</i>

00:15:39.550 --> 00:15:42.620
<i>So it's his agile movements 
that make him like a hornet.</i>

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:45.630
You're not going anywhere!

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:50.090
I'm the man who climbs 
through sheer effort...

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:52.380
Teshima Junta!

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:56.720
<i>He's close!</i>

00:15:57.530 --> 00:15:58.560
<i>He's too close!</i>

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:02.060
<i>The shoulder?</i>

00:16:02.490 --> 00:16:03.810
Whoa!

00:16:05.220 --> 00:16:06.060
Later.

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:08.860
Damn it.

00:16:12.590 --> 00:16:14.140
<i>He's gone.</i>

00:16:14.140 --> 00:16:17.410
<i>I don't know what happened 
for a second there.</i>

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:20.270
<i>My entire body was pushed 
off the asphalt.</i>

00:16:21.740 --> 00:16:22.750
<i>His speed...</i>

00:16:23.330 --> 00:16:24.490
<i>His timing...</i>

00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:28.900
<i>In the time it took me to do 
one thing, he was doing five.</i>

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:30.590
<i>Not only that...</i>

00:16:31.110 --> 00:16:33.510
<i>But he did it without mercy or hesitation.</i>

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:36.890
#5 has fallen.

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:39.810
<i>That's the Peak Hornet...</i>

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:41.470
<i>Damn.</i>

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:44.810
<i>Watch out, Onoda!</i>

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:54.860
It's already time for our race.

00:16:55.180 --> 00:16:56.930
<i>Shinkai-kun?</i>

00:16:56.930 --> 00:16:58.870
<i>Huh? What's he doing there?</i>

00:16:59.340 --> 00:17:03.130
Let's race, Mountain King.

00:17:04.170 --> 00:17:07.460
Is your answer "yes"?

00:17:08.100 --> 00:17:12.420
<i>Teshima-san said he'd stop him, but...</i>

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:14.950
Um, Teshi—

00:17:14.950 --> 00:17:15.680
Teshi?

00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:20.140
Oh, Teshima-san. You mean #5?

00:17:20.670 --> 00:17:22.090
He...

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:27.330
...fell behind while chatting.

00:17:27.330 --> 00:17:29.260
I broke past him easily.

00:17:32.050 --> 00:17:33.360
<i>He caught up to me!</i>

00:17:34.690 --> 00:17:35.940
<i>He's close!</i>

00:17:35.940 --> 00:17:37.300
Until we reach them.

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:38.150
Huh?

00:17:38.150 --> 00:17:40.580
We'll see who reaches the front first.

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:41.980
How does that sound?

00:17:43.930 --> 00:17:47.230
You're going to reach them 
before Hakone Academy, right?

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:48.980
Aren't those your orders?

00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:52.770
Forget about rules and games.

00:17:52.770 --> 00:17:53.920
You understand, don't you?

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:56.340
This is a race.

00:17:58.220 --> 00:18:03.930
Your strategy requires you to 
stop me and reach your team first.

00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:08.140
Otherwise, your loss is certain.

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:13.890
You have no choice but to fight me.

00:18:14.330 --> 00:18:17.360
Now, let's race. Your answer...

00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:19.360
It's "yes," isn't it?

00:18:20.460 --> 00:18:21.700
<i>When did he...</i>

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:28.920
The race has already begun!

00:18:29.950 --> 00:18:30.880
He's fast!

00:18:32.100 --> 00:18:33.170
<i>He's gone.</i>

00:18:34.030 --> 00:18:35.800
<i>I need to catch up.</i>

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:37.730
<i>Shinkai-kun...</i>

00:18:38.290 --> 00:18:40.430
<i>He's fast. He's strong.</i>

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:42.100
<i>But...</i>

00:18:42.490 --> 00:18:44.390
You have to go on alone!

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:45.560
Yes, sir!

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:47.770
You're #1.

00:18:48.170 --> 00:18:50.440
You have a job to do.

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:51.560
Yes, sir!

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:54.320
What did you learn from Makishima-san?

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:55.570
Yes, sir!

00:18:55.570 --> 00:19:00.070
Ride as hard as you can to 
reach Imaizumi and Naruko!

00:19:01.230 --> 00:19:01.780
Yes, sir!

00:19:04.670 --> 00:19:05.850
<i>Shinkai-kun...</i>

00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:09.910
<i>I'll pass you and reach the front!</i>

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:13.290
Think you can't do what you did last year?

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:17.070
Of course not.

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:19.450
Because you've gotten stronger.

00:19:23.020 --> 00:19:24.170
<i>Stronger!</i>

00:19:25.050 --> 00:19:27.930
I'm Kikuta from class 4. 
I'm on the baseball team.

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:29.770
Let's race.

00:19:30.210 --> 00:19:34.120
The bicycle club's the national 
champion, right? That's amazing.

00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:36.110
But I'm a regular and the 
king of stolen bases.

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:39.220
I-I'll pass. I doubt I'd stand a chance.

00:19:39.220 --> 00:19:39.820
What, what?

00:19:40.140 --> 00:19:42.030
You're racing Onoda-kun?

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:46.140
Whoever touches the knob
 of the door to the roof wins.

00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:48.160
What? B-But I...

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:49.450
Ready...

00:19:49.980 --> 00:19:50.960
Uh, but...

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:51.330
Go!

00:19:57.590 --> 00:20:03.110
<i>I always flinch when I hear the word "race."</i>

00:20:10.710 --> 00:20:12.690
Come on, give me everything you've got.

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:14.480
This isn't fun.

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:18.340
Huh? But I am trying.

00:20:19.370 --> 00:20:22.340
<i>Because I don't really like racing.</i>

00:20:23.850 --> 00:20:27.750
<i>I don't particularly like them,
 whether I win or lose.</i>

00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:30.500
<i>But...</i>

00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:33.210
<i>If you...</i>

00:20:33.990 --> 00:20:36.630
<i>If you're attacking the team
 Makishima-san entrusted to me...</i>

00:20:39.820 --> 00:20:45.680
<i>If you're going to attack
 Imaizumi-kun and Naruko-kun...</i>

00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:53.600
Then my answer to your challenge to a race...

00:20:54.610 --> 00:20:56.600
My answer is yes!

00:21:02.270 --> 00:21:05.410
<i>I thought that got me a hundred meters ahead.</i>

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:08.700
<i>But he's already caught up. Incredible.</i>

00:21:09.140 --> 00:21:10.900
<i>No wonder he's the Mountain King!</i>

00:21:11.570 --> 00:21:14.270
Man. Oh, man!

00:21:14.270 --> 00:21:16.040
Those eyes are fantastic!

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:19.050
They're full of fighting spirit!

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:23.170
Then show me!

00:21:25.210 --> 00:21:28.430
Show me the high-cadence climb 
I've heard so much about!

00:21:31.190 --> 00:21:32.430
<i>No way.</i>

00:21:33.070 --> 00:21:35.380
<i>What kind of climbing ability is that?</i>

00:21:36.050 --> 00:21:38.480
<i>It's even crazier than they say!</i>

00:21:38.870 --> 00:21:42.230
You're so strong! So strong, Mountain King!

00:21:43.180 --> 00:21:45.660
I won't let you go!

00:23:18.000 --> 00:23:21.500
<b>Sohoku
High
School
Bicycle
Club</b>

00:23:18.510 --> 00:23:20.140
La dee da da!

00:23:20.140 --> 00:23:24.900
The power hidden in the chest I hold!

00:23:24.900 --> 00:23:29.470
To a new world that's not on the route—

00:23:30.460 --> 00:23:32.100
A-Aoyagi...

00:23:32.100 --> 00:23:33.430
You, too?

00:23:35.300 --> 00:23:36.410
No!

00:23:36.580 --> 00:23:39.930
<i>NEXT LINE  Mountain King</i>

00:23:39.930 --> 00:23:44.940
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:51.250
<b>Don't miss the next episode</b>
